# =============================================================================
# Mini-SPOT — Environment Variables
# =============================================================================
# 1. Copy this file:
# 2. Fill in your DISPLAY value (see instructions below)
#
# FINDING YOUR DISPLAY VALUE:
#
#   Linux:
#     Run in terminal: echo $DISPLAY
#     Usually: :0 or :1
#     Example: DISPLAY=:0
#
#   macOS (XQuartz):
#     Install XQuartz from https://www.xquartz.org
#     Run: xhost +localhost
#     Then: echo $DISPLAY
#     Usually: /private/tmp/com.apple.launchd.xxx/org.xquartz:0
#     Example: DISPLAY=/private/tmp/com.apple.launchd.abc123/org.xquartz:0
#
#   Windows (VcXsrv):
#     Install VcXsrv from https://sourceforge.net/projects/vcxsrv
#     Launch XLaunch → check "Disable access control"
#     Set DISPLAY to your Windows host IP with :0
#     Find IP: run ipconfig in PowerShell, look for WSL adapter
#     Example: DISPLAY=172.20.0.1:0
# =============================================================================

#DISPLAY=:0
